-## Parent-owned constructor state (phase 1a)
+## Consolidated inheritance entry point
+
+PR #20865 combines direct GPUWorker inheritance with the interface quarantine
+from #20866, which it supersedes. It targets main directly. Phase 0 tooling and
+later migrations remain independent work.
+
+NPUWorker derives from GPUWorker and calls the real parent constructor through
+`super().__init__()`. The 54 existing non-constructor NPUWorker methods at baseline
+`28065346d433f9d23157c77c2b5b79c959a61871` retain their bodies, signatures and
+decorators. Execution, config updates, reload, model loading, dummy batches,
+sleep/wake and shutdown remain local. The old Phase 0.5 alignment and Phase 1b
+shutdown migration are excluded. NPU device/HCCL setup and the current V2,
+encoder-only, 310P and Xlite runner construction paths are retained.
+
+The dependency is verified vLLM main `24420b7a` plus constructor hooks from
+<https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/pull/65565>. The review pin is
+`e9f031bed0d150e2bef4b1eaa29aa50061e89203`. Missing hooks fail before parent
+construction. Merge the companion and update the pin to its merged commit
+before rollout. The matched v0.33.0 release needs the same hooks qualified or
+backported. There is no fallback that bypasses the parent constructor.
+
+## Parent construction
 
 | State | Ascend contract |
 | --- | --- |
-| Shared config and ranks | Initialized by the real GPU Worker constructor |
-| Float32 matmul precision | Adopt upstream `VLLM_FLOAT32_MATMUL_PRECISION` |
-| Elastic EP executor | Explicit unsupported executor, no CUDA imports or thread pool |
+| Shared config and ranks | Initialized by the actual GPUWorker constructor |
+| Float32 matmul precision | Adopt upstream configuration |
+| Elastic EP executor | Resource-free unsupported executor; no CUDA elastic EP imports |
 | Fault-tolerance sentinel | Reject enabled fault tolerance before parent construction |
-| Sleep buffer, parameter and draft dictionaries | Created by parent; NPU sleep retains its own policy |
-| Weight transfer engine and active/draft flags | Created by parent; transitions migrate in phase 3 |
-| Profiler config and wrapper | Validate NPU torch profiler through a constructor hook; create lazily |
-| PP send handles | Parent initializes the list; the existing Ascend send override is retained |
-| Sleep backend cache | Created by parent; CaMem integration follows in phase 3 |
-
-Current main uses V2, encoder-only, 310P and Xlite construction paths; their NPU
-device initialization is retained. Parent `init_device` is never called.
-Runtime startup and serving qualification remain required before merging this
-PR; portable contract tests are not a substitute for those checks.
+| Sleep buffer, parameter and draft dictionaries | Parent initializes state; existing NPU policy remains |
+| Weight transfer engine and active/draft flags | Parent initializes state; existing NPU update methods remain |
+| Profiler | NPU validation hook; wrapper remains lazily initialized |
+| PP send handles | Parent initializes state; existing NPU execution is retained |
+| Sleep backend cache | Parent initializes None; no GPU allocator is selected |
+
+Only `_make_elastic_ep_executor` and `_validate_profiler_config` are newly
+implemented hooks, because the parent constructor calls them. The executor
+rejects all work and permits repeated shutdown. The profiler hook accepts
+disabled profiling and the torch NPU profiler.
+
+Existing shutdown is retained: the unsupported executor allocates no thread
+pool or device resources, and the sleep backend remains uncreated. Changes to
+cleanup, PP handle ownership, decorators or runner contracts require separate
+validation and review. Parent `init_device` is never called.
+
+## Unverified interfaces
+
+All 29 other GPUWorker methods or properties newly visible at the pinned
+dependency are explicitly overridden to raise `NotImplementedError`, including
+private helpers and GPU defaults returning None, False or an empty result.
+The `sleep_mode_backend` and `randomize_dummy_inputs` property descriptors are
+preserved and raise on access.
+
+The complete immutable inventory is `UNVERIFIED_GPU_WORKER_METHODS` in
+`vllm_ascend/worker/worker_interfaces.py`:
+
+| Group | Interfaces |
+| --- | --- |
+| Execution hooks | `_before_execute_model`, `_get_pp_all_gather_group`, `_after_pp_send`, `annotate_profile` |
+| Sleep and draft helpers | `sleep_mode_backend`, `_get_sleep_parameters`, `discard`, `randomize_dummy_inputs`, `get_draft_model` |
+| Weight updates | `supports_draft_weight_updates`, `_set_draft_weight_update_target`, `shutdown_weight_transfer_engine`, `start_draft_weight_update`, `_start_weight_update` |
+| Initialization | `_init_workspace_and_model_runner`, `_make_model_runner` |
+| GPU compilation | `_scoped_allocator_max_split`, `_compile_or_warm_up_model`, `_maybe_activate_jit_monitor`, `_get_cudagraph_capture_context` |
+| Checkpoint and export | `checkpoint_prepare`, `checkpoint_restore`, `save_sharded_state`, `save_tensorized_model` |
+| Other control interfaces | `handle_ft_command`, `reset_mm_cache`, `get_compilation_match_table`, `get_encoder_timing_stats`, `elastic_ep_execute` |
+
+For each later migration, validate the NPU runner and supported vLLM contracts,
+remove the explicit stub and inventory entry together, and update the
+method-resolution guard to allow that verified inherited method. No earlier
+draft implementation is enabled by this change.
+
+## Validation
+
+Portable tests execute every rejection method and property without initialized
+Worker state and verify that the inventory exactly matches the explicit stubs.
+They also cover constructor structure, profiler settings and executor behavior.
+
+Runtime guards compare the actual installed GPUWorker surface with NPUWorker
+declarations. New upstream interfaces fail until an explicit boundary or a
+validated inheritance decision is supplied. Another test executes the real
+GPUWorker constructor on a bare NPUWorker with WorkerBase configuration setup
+replaced by a test double. This checks parent state and hook dispatch, not full
+NPU startup.
+
+Source comparison checks that all existing non-constructor methods and
+decorators remain unchanged. Actual startup, serving and the applicable
+hardware/version validation remain required before merge.
